Subject: [PATCH 00/24] ALSA: hda/ca0132: add Sound Blaster AE-9 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This series adds support for the Creative Sound Blaster AE-9 (PCI
1102:0010, subsystem 1102:0071): dual CA0132 codecs, an ES9038Q2M
headphone DAC, a SABRE9006 line-out DAC and the external Audio Control
Module (ACM).

It is based on the current sound.git for-next branch (Linux v7.2 plus
the later ca0132 changes, including the AE-5 LED strip work).  The first
patch is the base bring-up; the rest are split by feature so the
hardware protocol can be reviewed in order:

  - base quirk, PCI/pincfg, the Windows-style DSP/PLL/DAC/GPIO bring-up,
    the output-connect overlay and the ACM UART service;
  - output routing (including the ES9038 routing table on every
    switch), jack detection and auto-detect;
  - SBX light, knob/button handling and the 500 ms ACM service;
  - capture (secondary-codec line-in/S-PDIF and the opt-in main-codec
    microphone);
  - Direct Mode (stream-rate following) and the remaining mixer/display
    refinements.

The series depends on the HDA-core posted-write flush sent separately
("ALSA: hda: flush posted writes around the command ring setup");
without it probing the card hard-locks the machine.

Tested on the physical card and ACM with Fedora 44 / kernel 7.2.14:
playback at 44.1-192 kHz, capture from the ACM microphone, rear line-in,
What U Hear and optical S/PDIF at 44.1-192 kHz, optical loopback at all
rates, suspend/resume, and the knob/display/buttons.  All 24 patches
pass scripts/checkpatch.pl with no errors or warnings.

The firmware output-connect overlay is extracted from Creative's
Windows package at install time and is not part of this series.

DarkNikGr

DarkNikGr (24):
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: add Sound Blaster AE-9 support
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: keep the desktop's card profiles off the AE-9
    routing
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: no jack detection on the AE-9 headphone pin
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9 ACM: SBX light follows Enable OutFX, SBX button
    toggles it
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9 ACM: knob press = mute (display MUTE), medium
    press = output toggle
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: keep AE-9 capture opt-in
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: use system_dfl_wq for the ACM service
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9 output switching mutes the line-out buffer
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9 ACM: keep the knob/display path fast
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: allow capture on the secondary codec
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9 capture support (ACM mic + rear line-in)
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: hide the unwired Front Microphone input
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: enable What U Hear capture
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: Direct Mode rate following (44.1-192 kHz)
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: expose Direct Mode as a mixer control
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: Direct Mode effects-off, stereo constraint,
    unmute hook
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: bound the knob and button UART queries
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: auto-switch output on ACM headphone jack
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: share the headphone and line-out mixer control
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: align hardware gain and ACM volume display
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: honour the HP/Speaker auto-detect switch
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: refresh the ACM display on mixer changes
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: leave the AE-9 headphone gain to the ACM
  ALSA: hda/ca0132: fix the AE-5 headphone gain item names

